      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright Â© 2011 American Society for Surgery of the Hand. Published by Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Osteochondral lesions of the wrist are rare in the pediatric and adolescent population. We report a case of an osteochondral lesion of the lunate facet of the radiocarpal joint in a 6-year-old girl with chronic wrist pain after falling on her hand. Arthroscopic debridement of the osteochondral fragment relieved the symptoms and improved wrist function. Osteochondral lesions should be considered in the differential diagnosis of chronic wrist pain in children with a history of trauma."
      },
